           control in the same configuration that must forward zero. tcpdump is authoritative
           for what was on the wire; the two counters agreed exactly in every graded leg.

STEP 0 -- baseline (feature OFF)                                          done
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The TFS states the global default: "Forwarding remote DNS query feature is disabled". The
  static name-server is configured FIRST, before the DHCP client learns one, because
  S1570.1.12's "added last" ordering is untestable in any other sequence.

awplus(config)# ip name-server 192.168.48.9
awplus# show ip name-server
  Currently learned name-servers:
  192.168.48.2 dynamic (vlan48)
  192.168.48.9 static
                                             <-- both servers present before the feature is
                                                 enabled: one static, one already learned by
                                                 the DHCP client on vlan48

  The measured feature-OFF control -- five queries on the wire and zero forwarded -- is
  STEP 2, run on the identical bench after the feature had been shown working.

