STEP 4 -- which server the relay queries (S1570.1.12, ordering limb)      PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: `show ip name-server` CANNOT answer this. It groups by type -- it printed
  `192.168.48.2 dynamic` above `192.168.48.9 static` both before and after a re-lease, which
  is equally consistent with "grouped display" and with "dynamic really is first", and
  distinguishes neither. The discriminator is therefore which server the relay actually
  queries. Two responders were run on eth4 at once, each answering ARP for its own address and
  each returning a DIFFERENT A record:

      192.168.48.9  (static)         -> 10.9.9.9
      192.168.48.2  (DHCP-learned)   -> 10.2.2.2

  and one query for ck-order.test was sent from eth3.

  Leg `order`:

    .9 static : UPSTREAM QUERIES RECEIVED: 0   answered 0   arp answered 0
    .2 dynamic: UPSTREAM QUERIES RECEIVED: 1   answered 1   arp answered 1
        t=26.8217  ck-order.test  from 192.168.48.100
    tcpdump eth4:
        17:01:54.804064 IP 192.168.48.100.50058 > 192.168.48.2.53: A? ck-order.test.
        17:01:54.883288 IP 192.168.48.2.53 > 192.168.48.100.50058: 1/0/0 A 10.2.2.2
    client received: ck-order.test -> 10.2.2.2
                                             <-- the DUT queried ONLY the DHCP-learned
                                                 server, and did not even ARP for the static
                                                 one

  Control, to separate "the static server was not preferred" from "the static server was
  unreachable". Same bench, same addressing; only the DHCP-learned entry is removed, by
  re-leasing from a DHCP server that offers NO option 6:

awplus# show ip name-server
  Currently learned name-servers:
  192.168.48.9 static
awplus# show ip interface brief
  Interface             IP-Address         Status          Protocol
  vlan10                192.168.10.1/24    admin up        running
  vlan48                192.168.48.100/24  admin up        running
                                             <-- still addressed; only the dynamic entry is
                                                 gone

  Leg `ctl2`, 6 queries:

    .9 static : UPSTREAM QUERIES RECEIVED: 4   answered 4   arp answered 1
    tcpdump eth4:
        17:05:43.998660 ARP, Request who-has 192.168.48.9 tell 192.168.48.100
        17:05:44.031007 ARP, Reply 192.168.48.9 is-at 00:0d:b9:55:77:0f
        17:05:44.031306 IP 192.168.48.100.49266 > 192.168.48.9.53: A? ck-a.test.
        17:05:44.119328 IP 192.168.48.9.53 > 192.168.48.100.49266: 1/0/0 A 10.9.9.9

  => STEP 4 PASS: the DHCP-learned server is genuinely the one the relay uses, which is what
     this limb of S1570.1.12 is for -- the import is functional, not cosmetic. The pair also
     establishes a real behaviour worth recording: with BOTH a static and a DHCP-learned
     server configured, this DUT sends its query to the DHCP-learned one and never consults
     the static one, although the control proves the static one at .9 is perfectly reachable
     and is used the moment it is the only server. That is not graded as a failure, because
     the TFS's "added last of configured name-server list" describes LIST POSITION and a
     resolver is not obliged to walk its list in order; it may select by responsiveness or by
     most-recent-update. The measurement establishes the externally visible preference only --
     see the CAVEAT. Either the list order differs from the spec, or "added last" describes
     storage rather than query order and the spec could say so.

